Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:00:02 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 91/91] XHTTP: Close test clients with their test

newFlowTestClient left its governed connections to the server's close:
each released its flowGroup only once its read loop saw EOF, which can
come after the test returns, and TestFlowGroupShared, which runs next,
found the group. The helper now takes the test and closes its transport
and connections in a cleanup registered when it makes them;
flowConn.Close releases the group before it returns.
TestH2WindowsEndToEnd, which dials governed connections itself, does the
same. On one CPU, each client test before TestFlowGroupShared, ten
times: four of them left a group in 2 to 8 of 10 runs before, none
after.
